fuser on Radix (ADR 0226), for programs that serve a filesystem through
/devices/fuse in Linux's FUSE protocol: on nix 0.30, which the port
patches for Radix, in place of 0.29; Linux's errno for a missing extended
attribute (ENODATA), as Radix's numbers are Linux's; each answer written
in one write, which /devices/fuse needs and Radix's writev makes only up
to PIPE_BUF; and no mount of its own. Radix mounts a connection with
radix-directory(2)'s mount_fuse, which `mount -t` makes, and the program
serves the descriptor it is handed with Session::from_fd; Session::new and
spawn_mount2 say so.

